---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LineChart from "../components/LineChart.astro";
import PeriodTable from "../components/PeriodTable.astro";
import { series, latest } from "../lib/data.js";
import { num, period } from "../lib/format.js";
const fd = latest(series("cga_fiscal_deficit_pct_be"));
const fdPrev = latest(series("cga_fiscal_deficit_pct_be_prev"));
const gst = latest(series("gst_gross_collections"));
import fs from "node:fs";
const budget = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync("src/data/generated/budget.json", "utf8"));
---
<Base current="fiscal" title="Fiscal">
  <h1>Fiscal</h1>
  <p class="lede">Is the Union government on track for its budgeted deficit? By the end of {period(fd.period, "M")} the fiscal deficit had reached {num(fd.value, 1)}% of the year's Budget Estimate, against {num(fdPrev.value, 1)}% at the same point last year. Monthly accounts from the Controller General of Accounts; GST from the GST portal.</p>

  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Fiscal deficit, year to date, as % of the Budget Estimate" subtitle="Each financial year starts in April; March is the full year (% of Revised Estimates)"
      lines={[{ id: "cga_fiscal_deficit_pct_be", label: "This year" }, { id: "cga_fiscal_deficit_pct_be_prev", label: "Same month, previous year" }]} years={2} />
    <LineChart title="Capital expenditure, year to date, as % of the Budget Estimate" subtitle="March is the full year (% of Revised Estimates)"
      lines={[{ id: "cga_capex_pct_be", label: "This year" }, { id: "cga_capex_pct_be_prev", label: "Same month, previous year" }]} years={2} />
  </div>

  {budget.rows.length > 0 && <>
  <h2 id="budget">Union Budget {budget.year} at a glance</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th>₹ lakh crore</th>{budget.columns.map((c) => <th>{c}</th>)}<th>BE vs last RE</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {budget.rows.map((r) => <tr><td>{r.item}</td>{r.values.map((v) => <td>{v === null ? "–" : r.ratio ? `${num(v, 1)}%` : num(v, 2)}</td>)}
        <td>{r.change_pct === null ? "" : `${r.change_pct > 0 ? "+" : ""}${num(r.change_pct, 1)}%`}</td></tr>)}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="chart-sub">BE: Budget Estimates, presented with the Budget; RE: Revised Estimates for the year then ending; Actuals: audited outturn. "BE vs last RE" is the planned change on the year before's revised figure (site calculation). Effective capital expenditure is capital expenditure plus grants-in-aid for creating capital assets, as defined in the Budget. Deficit ratios are % of GDP as printed. Source: Ministry of Finance, Budget at a Glance.</p>
  </>}

  <h2 id="accounts">Union government accounts, year to date</h2>
  <PeriodTable heading="₹ lakh crore, April to the month shown" n={6} digits={2} rows={[
    { id: "cga_total_receipts_fytd" }, { id: "cga_revenue_receipts_fytd", indent: true }, { id: "cga_net_tax_fytd", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_total_expenditure_fytd" }, { id: "cga_revenue_expenditure_fytd", indent: true }, { id: "cga_interest_fytd", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_capex_fytd", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_fiscal_deficit_fytd" }, { id: "cga_revenue_deficit_fytd" }, { id: "cga_primary_deficit_fytd" },
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Cumulative from April, so values reset each financial year. CGA cautions that the deficit in the monthly accounts during the year is not necessarily an indicator of the deficit for the full year.</p>

  <h2 id="gst">GST collections</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="GST collections" subtitle="₹ lakh crore per month" lines={[{ id: "gst_gross_collections", label: "Gross" }, { id: "gst_net_collections", label: "Net of refunds" }]} years={3} />
    <LineChart title="GST growth" subtitle="% change on the same month a year earlier (same-definition comparison)" lines={[{ id: "gst_gross_growth", label: "Gross" }, { id: "gst_net_growth", label: "Net" }]} years={3} />
  </div>
  <p class="chart-sub">GST portal statistics workbook; provisional. Gross collections in {period(gst.period, "M")}: ₹{num(gst.value, 2)} lakh crore. Each year's growth compares like with like (later months exclude compensation cess on both sides). January 2025 is missing because that month's sheet in the source workbook is malformed.</p>

  <h2 id="taxes">Tax collections by head</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Direct taxes, year to date" subtitle="Corporate tax plus income tax, % change on the same months a year earlier"
      lines={[{ id: "cga_direct_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", label: "Direct taxes" }, { id: "cga_gross_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", label: "Gross tax revenue" }]} years={4} />
    <LineChart title="Corporate and income tax, year to date" subtitle="% change on the same months a year earlier"
      lines={[{ id: "cga_corporate_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", label: "Corporate tax" }, { id: "cga_income_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", label: "Income tax" }]} years={4} />
  </div>
  <PeriodTable heading="₹ lakh crore, April to the month shown" n={6} digits={2} rows={[
    { id: "cga_gross_tax_fytd" }, { id: "cga_direct_tax_fytd", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_corporate_tax_fytd", indent: true }, { id: "cga_income_tax_fytd", indent: true }, { id: "cga_stt_fytd", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_customs_fytd", indent: true }, { id: "cga_excise_fytd", indent: true },
  ]} />
  <PeriodTable heading="% change on the same months a year earlier" n={6} rows={[
    { id: "cga_gross_tax_fytd", how: "yoy" }, { id: "cga_direct_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_corporate_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", indent: true }, { id: "cga_income_tax_fytd", how: "yoy", indent: true },
    { id: "cga_customs_fytd", how: "yoy", indent: true },
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">CGA monthly trend of tax revenue: gross collections by head, before the states' share is assigned. "Direct taxes" here is a site calculation, corporate tax plus taxes on income other than corporate tax; securities transaction tax is shown separately and has its own head only from FY 2023-24. Year-to-date growth in April and May swings widely because refunds can exceed collections early in the year (corporate tax was negative in April 2015 and April 2016). Excise is left out of the growth table because its April collections are close to zero (₹−39 crore in April 2025), which makes its year-to-date growth meaningless for months. Corporate tax arrives mostly in June, September, December and March (the advance-tax months: in FY 2025-26 these four months brought in about four-fifths of the year's corporate tax), so growth is best compared at those months.</p>

  <h2>Still to come on this page</h2>
  <p class="chart-sub">General government (Centre plus states) deficit and debt, state finances, and a longer history of Budget numbers (each Budget adds a year). Checklist: docs/guidebook/05-pages/fiscal.md.</p>
</Base>
